Chaos harness for soak lab

This directory contains simple mock services and orchestration to simulate hostile behaviors.

Files:
- otlp_hang.py: an HTTP server that accepts OTLP HTTP requests and hangs (never responds) to simulate a stuck collector.
- bad_backend.py: a small TCP/HTTP server that can simulate slow backends, partial headers, malformed chunked encoding, and abrupt connection closes.
- run_chaos.sh: orchestrates a chaos run by bringing up services and exercising scenarios.

Usage (from soak):

  # Replace ferron config and start chaos compose
  cd soak
  ./chaos/run_chaos.sh

Scenarios available on the bad backend (http://bad-backend:8000):
- /slow?delay=10       - respond after <delay> seconds
- /close_mid           - send partial body then close connection
- /partial_headers     - slowly stream headers (slowloris-like)
- /malformed_chunked   - respond with invalid chunked encoding

Notes:
- run_chaos.sh uses docker-compose override file docker-compose.chaos.yml which mounts the chaos scripts into the Python containers.
- The script will copy ferron-chaos.conf to ferron-test.conf used by the compose file.
- Use this harness to validate graceful degradation, queue/backpressure behavior, and logging when backends or exporters misbehave.
